and leverages per-target feature sets, addressing the core issue of MLP memorization (train loss 0.42 vs val MA-RAE 21+).", "training_evaluation": "Implement stratified 5-fold cross-validation based on target missingness pattern using GroupKFold as before but with groups derived from per-target missingness (create a binary pattern per sample). For each fold, split into train/validation for early stopping. After CV, retrain each LightGBM on full training data. For inference, apply the same per-target feature selection and predict using the individual models, then calibrate with the meta-model. Clip final predictions to physically plausible ranges as in current code. This training strategy directly mirrors historical successful gradient boosting ensembles for sparse multi-target regression."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
